8. NOT MEASURED / OUT OF SCOPE FOR THIS AUDIT

  * No exploit payload was built or sent. Nothing here is a PoC; the "live"
    judgements in section 4 are the prerequisites (version, SAPI, ini values,
    pool size, upload handling) each confirmed by its own command, plus the
    vendor/CNCERT statement that the path is pre-script.
  * No production host was inspected. If the real deployment runs a distro PHP
    with a backported fix, its `php -v` will still look vulnerable; check the
    distro advisory before applying section 5 row 3.
  * PHP 5.x: affected per the published version ranges; no upstream fix exists
    and none was tested here (no php5 image was run).
  * CVSS was not recomputed for these layouts. The vendor score is 9.2 for the
    interpreter; a per-layout score for FreeMED would be a separate exercise.
  * xdebug being loaded in a production image (section 3) is noted as incident-
    al hardening debt, not assessed further here.


