10. REMEDIATION LANDED (2026-10-24)

  Measured evidence for every row in this section, with the commands that
  produced it: tests/security/evidence/php2shell-remediation.txt.

  (a) INTERPRETER. docker/Dockerfile is new: FROM php:8.3.36-fpm pinned by
      digest (php@sha256:c435accaeb7c535cacf8d6d188fc310431f4fc54545b1694a7930
      69185271dcb, the digest php:8.3-fpm resolved to on 2026-10-23), extensions
      exif/gd/intl/mysqli/opcache/soap/sodium/xsl/zip, xdebug deliberately NOT
      installed, and a build-time assertion that fails the build when
      version_compare(PHP_VERSION, "8.3.36", ">=") is false. The image labels
      record the version and both CVE ids so `docker inspect` can answer
      "what interpreter is this" without a shell. docker/docker-compose.yml now
      builds that file as freemed-php:8.3.36 instead of pulling
      jbuchbinder/moodle-php-8.3-fpm:latest, and pins the database at
      mariadb:10.11 (the tree's schema is measured there; `latest` has been
      measured to leave ~35 tables uncreated).

      Measured: image `php -v` = PHP 8.3.36; old image 8.3.31.

  (b) INI MOUNT. docker/docker-compose.yml mounts the file at
      /usr/local/etc/php/conf.d/zz-freemed.ini, the directory the image
      actually scans. Measured after the change: `php --ini` lists
      zz-freemed.ini, and the values read back are the file's values
      (section 3.1's ablation now passes in the other direction).

  (c) MITIGATION LINES. docker/php-custom.ini carries
      session.upload_progress.enabled = Off and fatal_error_backtraces = 0
      (the second is an 8.5 directive; on 8.3 it is accepted and ignored,
      measured: ini_get() returns false and there is no diagnostic). Also in
      that file, two pre-existing defects are corrected: `max_file_uploads =
      128M` (a COUNT of files, so 128M was being read as 134217728) is now
      `128`, and the Apache-only `php_value[memory_limit]` line, inert in an
      ini file, is removed. post_max_size is set explicitly to 64M - the value
      lib/freemed.php asks for, though its ini_set() at request time cannot
      deliver it (post_max_size is PHP_INI_PERDIR).

      Measured on the live FPM SAPI through the shipped compose stack:
      session.upload_progress.enabled = "" (Off), register_argc_argv = "" (Off),
      post_max_size = 64M, memory_limit = 2048M, max_file_uploads = 128,
      mysqli loaded.

  (d) BODY CAPS. docker/nginx.conf client_max_body_size 10000M -> 64M;
      doc/freemed.apache.conf gains LimitRequestBody 67108864 inside the
      /usr/share/freemed <Directory>, plus the two ini lines an operator must
      put in the SYSTEM php.ini (not a <Directory>, which is applied after the
      request is parsed). Both are matched to PHP's post_max_size.

      Measured: a 70 MiB multipart upload through the shipped nginx now
      answers 413; a 1 MiB multipart upload still parses ($_FILES populated,
      error 0), so the mitigation did not break uploads. The existing
      hardening rules are unchanged and still answer 403 for /lib/API.php and
      for a PATH_INFO traversal.

  (e) DEBIAN. debian/control now depends on php8.3-mysql, php8.3-cgi, php8.3-gd,
      php8.3-curl, php8.3-cli, php8.3-dev and libapache2-mod-php8.3 instead of
      the php5 equivalents. Non-PHP debt in that file (mysql-server-5.1,
      openjdk-6-jdk, cupsys, tetex) is untouched and remains a packaging
      problem of its own; this change removes the interpreter that has no
      upstream fix, not every stale dependency.

  (f) GATES. scripts/php-runtime-check.sh asserts the SAPI is at or above the
      fix floor, with exit 0 / 1 (vulnerable) / 2 (INCONCLUSIVE - never a
      pass) and a --self-test that pins the comparison. It runs as part of
      `make security-check`, using PHP_IMAGE (php:8.3-cli) when the host has no
      php. Measured: exit 1 against 8.3.35, exit 0 against 8.3.36, and the
      self-test's seven rows pass. The harness images are rebuilt at 8.3.36
      (the 8.3.35 builds are kept as :8.3.35-apache / :8.3.35-fpm so the
      "gate bites" row stays reproducible).

  STILL OPEN, and not something this pass could close:

  * A production host has to be re-created from the new image; an fpm worker
    already running keeps the old binary resident until it is replaced. This
    repository cannot do that step, and nothing here proves any particular
    deployment has done it.
  * A distro PHP with a backported fix is invisible to a version check. The
    front-end layout in row 3 of section 5 is still the operator's problem,
    now with the body cap and the ini lines in the file they copy.
  * The upstream pattern the vendors patched around (state metadata updated
    before the allocation it describes) is still present in 8.3.36; the
    vendors themselves expect further instances. This audit closes the two
    published CVEs, not the class.

